# Design Binding — stitch

`DESIGN.md` `## Screens × form factors` lists component **names** only. The per-element detail
— text labels, badges, hint text, timestamp **format**, app-shell chrome, control order — lives in
the Stitch screen the table links to. Implementing from the name list alone drops elements
silently. This skill closes that gap.

The agent has already read `DESIGN.md`. For every screen a UI task implements (plan time) or has
implemented (implement time), run the three steps below. Read-only on Stitch — never edit screens.

## Step 1 — Locate the artifact

In `DESIGN.md § Screens × form factors`, each screen row links to a Stitch screen. Two access
paths, depending on the calling agent's tools:

- **Caller has `mcp__stitch__*`** (e.g. a design-review agent): fetch the screen via
  `mcp__stitch__get_screen` (returns screen content + shareable URL). Full element diff (Step 2,
  MCP path).
- **Caller lacks Stitch MCP** (the default impl-planning-agent / implementation-agent — Read/Write/
  Edit/Bash/Grep/Glob only, no MCP): you cannot fetch the live screen. Use `DESIGN.md`'s per-screen
  element detail (Step 2, DESIGN.md path) and raise the not-auto-verified flag in Step 3.

## Step 2 — Build the element manifest

**MCP path** — from `get_screen` content, enumerate the rendered elements (text, components,
layout order).

**DESIGN.md path** — read every per-screen element detail DESIGN.md carries. Coarser than the live
screen — flag accordingly.

Either path produces an ordered list per screen of every user-visible element:

- text labels + exact copy · badges / chips · hint / helper / error text
- timestamps **and their format** (relative vs absolute) · icons + accessible labels
- sub-components nested in a row / card — including a child a later feature added to an
  earlier-feature component (e.g. a badge on an existing list row)
- app-shell chrome: header, page title, nav, toolbar buttons + labels
- control order within a group (e.g. Save before Cancel)

## Step 3 — Diff against the code + flag

For each manifest element, confirm the implemented component renders it (or, at plan time, that a
task covers it). For any element present but absent from the code **and** not in the task scope /
PLAN.md file plan, append to `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/FLAGS.md` (create if absent):

```
### AF-<next>: inconsistency · task: T-NN · <code-file>
design element "<element>" on screen <S> present in Stitch screen but not implemented — DESIGN.md component list omitted it.
```

**DESIGN.md path** (caller lacked Stitch MCP): additionally raise ONE flag per screen

```
### AF-<next>: risky-pattern · task: T-NN · docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md
visual fidelity for screen <S> not auto-verified — implementation agent has no Stitch MCP access; diffed against DESIGN.md detail only, which may under-specify elements. Confirm by eye at /arh-human-review.
```

`<next>` is the next sequential AF id. Triaged at `/arh-human-review` before commit-PR. Never silently
skip an element because the component "looks done."

## Contract (uniform across all design providers)

- **Input:** `DESIGN.md` (already read) + the Stitch screen (or DESIGN.md detail when MCP-less).
- **Output:** zero or more `AF-NN` flags; the UI verified element-complete against the artifact.
- **Read-only** on the design source. Never weaken: a missing element is always a flag.

